[Music]  this is an updated version of the build  I created just before taking a six-month  break from the division after the  release of 1.7 I jumped into the game  with my old PvE build already equipped  so I decided to try it out and see if it  was still relevant with a few tweaks I  can honestly say that in my opinion this  is still the best easiest build for  taking on the PvE content in the  division I'm not claiming this is the  fastest build the clearing content and  when it comes to pc players there's a  few other options out there but when  you're on console and your aim is as  inconsistent as mine this build will  help clear even the most difficult PvE  content in the game I've used this with  challenging missions underground light  zone farming incursions and even soloing  legendary missions much like in 1.6  stacking towards skill power is the way  to go sure dispelled you're a little bit  squishy and your DPS in a little bit low  but that's okay cuz your skills are  doing most of the damage for you when it  comes to the most difficult PvE content  the difference between 500k toughness  and 300k toughness is a fraction of a  second when under heavy NPC fire why not  deploy something to be doing slash  taking the damage for you while you sit  safely at the distance as with all of my  builds videos I'll be trying to keep  this as clear and concise as possible I  will never state that you need to match  everything I've added to the build and  instead the idea is for you to use this  as a starting point or a template for  your own build change things up and  personalize it for your style play this  build consists of four piece by quest  and two piece technicians as I said  earlier the idea is to have your skills  doing and taking most of the damage  however with the right talents you'll be  able to do a decent amount of damage  with your weapons too as long as you  keep a little distance between yourself  in the enemy all gear pieces have been  rolled into skill power and all major  attributes skill power or skill haste  first or to help the Commuter of these  are available all mods should be  electronics with a skill haste as the  attribute applying the above should  leave you with around  8900 electronics and 45 to 50% skill  haste the equipped skills are flame  turrets and air both seeker Minds if  seeker mines have had a big nerf in 1.7  but they're still extremely useful in  hunting down in exposing hidden enemies  and slowing down shotgun rushes the bulk  of your skill damage will  coming from the turret however the key  to this build is via both the turret and  seeker mind will ignite enemies and by  using the following talents you'll  ensure that most enemies in front of you  will be on fires and majority of the  time the two talents I would call a must  are wild fire to have the vice bridge  more targets and tech support to keep  your turret active for longer the other  two slots are optional  here I'm using critical safe and steady  hands but in a team situation you may  want Combat Medic the primary weapon I'm  using is the urban India this weapon  synergizes so well with this build  because of the india's unique talent  distracted your damage is increased by  18 percent against targets with status  affects everything you're doing with  this builds causes fire status effects  so you actually end up getting a decent  amount of damage out of this weapon even  with nothing put into firearms the MDR  can be a bit of a pain to get used to on  console and it certainly isn't required  in order to have the cells work but  whatever you'd use I'd recommend rolling  talented onto the weapon although this  talent specifically says that killing a  target with this weapon increases skill  power by 15% for 20 seconds your skills  will also progress talent so as long as  you have a turret out this talent will  be permanently active the secondary  weapon has two purposes one is for range  as you want to be sitting back from the  fight and the other for healing here I  have the m700 the talents include  talented again and predatory this is  your primary way of healing but this  build  much like talent if you don't need to be  shooting the enemies to prop us if your  turret and seeker mines are getting  kills you'll be healing at the end of  this video I've included a cheat sheet  or quick reference guide that sums up  this build and everything I've covered  check it out and see what you think if  this has seemed a little bit complex or  you don't have a lot of the gear  mentioned in this video check out a  video my mate  average ant is released he'll be showing  you a build more directed at the casual  player it may not get you quite the same  stats but it'll certainly help you keep  up with the big boys in the in-game  content a link to the video should be on  screen right now but this channel will  also be included in this description  below I'll leave you with a little bit  of gameplay right now but if you'd like  to see more of this type of content from  us subscribe to the channel and leave a  comment below thanks  keep your heads down and keep it quiet  moaning hostiles detected the escort  party is taking heavy fire from the roof  another shot is you just do it  [Music]  make a bet like you  damn it oh my god  morning additional hospital team coming  [Music]  and  good morning additional hostile team  coming you want to are to back  [Music]  got the medic stink way across candle  and all staff accounted for no  casualties  [Music]

